comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-27T21:20:34.332Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: all-status searches for Sentry 11 major migration and Sentry 11.0.0 found historical closed 10.x refresh and telemetry items but no major-upgrade owner. Registry metadata: @sentry/node latest 11.0.0, released 2026-09-23T12:38:30.858Z; engine range includes supported Node >=22.18.0. This item is open and unclaimed until the seven-day release-age policy allows adoption."
  "2026-10-02T20:59:17.260Z","harness:codex","Live October 2 census: latest Sentry Node is 11.2.0, published October 1 at 11:12:16 UTC and below the seven-day adoption window. The older 11.0 line may now meet release age, but major adoption still needs this owner compatibility, installed-consumer and actual telemetry proof; it is not claimed complete or actively worked in PR 1375. Preserve this canonical open migration rather than importing a new duplicate."
  "2026-10-05T04:51:55.774Z","harness:codex","New GitHub intake 2026-10-05: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1403 proposes Sentry Node 11.0.0 from 10.75.1. Reused this canonical open migration after full live metadata and all-status intake. Registry confirms 11.0.0 release 2026-09-23T12:38:30.858Z is old enough; latest 11.4.0 published 2026-10-02T16:37:53.815Z remains below seven days. Age is not the missing acceptance for 11.0.0: its documented breaking instrumentation/configuration and more permissive data-collection defaults still require the owner privacy classification and real Node/Bun/telemetry migration proof. Current production Sentry has zero recent critical/high issues and required telemetry passes. PR 1403 is closed with a canonical PM link as deferred major migration rather than silently installed or falsely claimed incompatible. This owner remains open and unclaimed; no ignore rule or security/cooldown bypass is added."
  "2026-10-10T04:46:25.999Z","harness:codex","Fresh 2026-10-10 public registry census: Sentry Node latest 11.6.0 was published 2026-10-08T15:06:02.707Z and remains below the seven-day adoption window. Older 11.4.0 is old enough, but this owner still requires the recorded major privacy/configuration and real supported-consumer/telemetry acceptance. No age, safety, SDK or telemetry compatibility is inferred from semver eligibility. Current pinned 10.75.1 has no known audit vulnerability and the required Sentry/telemetry gate passes; the existing major-migration owner remains open and unclaimed."
  "2026-10-11T16:03:05.071Z","harness:codex","Live 2026-10-11 registry and production check: latest Sentry Node 11.6.0 was published 2026-10-08T15:06:02.707Z and remains below the unchanged seven-day adoption window. Current full dependency audit reports no known vulnerabilities; live required Sentry/telemetry gate reports zero recent critical/high blockers, 2.93 percent seven-day finish errors and zero missing-code rows. Retain this canonical major/privacy/telemetry migration without claiming implementation acceptance or creating a duplicate."
  "2026-10-12T13:18:59.178Z","harness:codex","Fresh 2026-10-12 Dependabot PR 1448 proposes 11.4.0 from 10.75.1. Reused this fully read canonical major-migration owner, including previous comments, resolution and history. Although 11.4.0 meets age, its major privacy/instrumentation acceptance remains open; the current connected delivery adopts eligible compatible 10.76.0 with zero known audit vulnerabilities. PR 1448 is deferred with this owner link rather than mislabeled as incompatible or complete; this item stays open and unclaimed."
  "2026-10-12T23:01:15.948Z","harness:codex","Dependency recheck October12: registry latest Sentry11.6.0 is4.33 days old and has not met the repository seven-day minimum. Current10.76.0 remains audit-clean. Retain this existing major migration owner open/unclaimed; adoption requires its privacy, instrumentation and installed-consumer proof even after cooldown."
  "2026-10-13T04:40:55.024Z","harness:codex","Implementation started alongside pm-58yzil: select the newest exact Sentry11 release older than seven days using fresh public registry timestamps; inspect installed types and upstream migration for dataCollection defaults and span-streaming hooks before mutation. Prior pinned10.76.0 remains rollback target. No publication or compatibility is inferred from version age."
  "2026-10-13T04:49:49.088Z","harness:codex","Migration acceptance refused by real packed-artifact gate. Exact11.4.0 passes source typecheck and66 focused Sentry tests; Babel7.29.7 as a root development peer resolves the Stryker8 mismatch without changing Stryker. However portable package distribution refuses Missing tested runtime package: @oxc-parser/binding-android-arm-eabi, introduced by Sentry11 bundler-plugin/native-parser dependencies. Runtime ledger expands to129 packages; a host install cannot supply every optional native platform artifact. Preserve artifact ceilings and full locked runtime inventory. Revert dependency migration and return this item open/unclaimed; resolving portable native optional distribution is required before adoption. No claimed major incompatibility from unit tests or age."
  "2026-10-14T04:36:58.187Z","harness:codex","October14 census: latest Sentry11.7.0 is1.5days old, below seven-day adoption. Full live item records the separate portable optional-native-artifact blocker for the older11.4.0 attempt. Preserve10.76.0 as the supported transport; do not retry a known-invalid artifact or describe the newer release as eligible."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text,edited_at}:
  "2026-09-28T05:51:10.872Z","harness:codex","Readiness repair 2026-09-28: the complete active census found this as the sole item lacking acceptance criteria, estimate, risk, confidence and expected result. The 240-minute estimate covers compatibility investigation and verification, not a promised delivery date. Earliest adoption remains seven complete days after the recorded upstream release (2026-09-30T12:38:30.858Z), with live registry revalidation before dependency changes.","2026-09-28T07:22:06.053Z"
